// SDF round
//
// Inflates a field by `radius`: every surface moves outward that far, and
// sharp corners become rounded ones of that radius. A negative radius
// shrinks the field instead.
//
// Unlike a smoothing operator this keeps the boundary exactly where it
// promises, which is why it is the cheap way to bevel a composition.
fn sdf_round(
    distance: f32, // A signed distance field. @default 0.0
    radius: f32,   // How far to grow (negative shrinks). @default 0.1
) -> f32 {
    return distance - radius;
}
